{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774748,"nonce":"pxvz/kjoQImJrBNsz5syK9b3Vts=","title":"Committed-pack expiry + RetentionProfile: the retention story's last leg (6499fb1, 82c5775)","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #102 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `feat/6499fb1-committed-expiry` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-08-26T00:15:31Z · Merged: 2026-08-26T12:44:46Z\n\nThe last leg of the retention story (git-bug `6499fb1` + `82c5775`): the pass that deletes committed pack data, and the `RetentionProfile` that decides when. **911/911 green, twice** (real PG + MinIO). Full chain: plan → skeptical audit → independent judge → build → review — and the chain earned it again:\n\n- **The audit** found three holes in the plan: pinned pre-epoch runs losing their durable backing (the record sweep drains the epoch floor while pins keep roots served for years), an ADR-0056 rerun flipping a run non-terminal between candidate SELECT and the victim transaction, and committed-recordless packs leaking forever.\n- **The judge** replaced two proposed patches with one lemma: *a pre-epoch borrower's owners are necessarily pre-epoch* — so the floor scopes to pre-epoch victims only (post-epoch content expires on borrow edges from day one), becomes a control-plane **reachability** check (no pre-epoch run non-terminal / within workspace TTL / pinned), and the recordless arm folds under the same predicate.\n\n**What ships:**\n- `depot_expiry.rs` (control-plane side — victim selection is run policy; the Depot keeps owning bytes): per-victim single transaction under the reclaimer's advisory lock — `FOR UPDATE` the fence's packs, re-read the full candidate predicate in-txn (terminal + past-TTL + unpinned; catches mid-pass reruns), borrower `NOT EXISTS` on the #101 ledger, delete the four row families, pointers only. Bytes flow through the shipped rowless reclaimer a cadence later. `40P01` aborts the pass.\n- **`RetentionProfile`** (TTL-only, deliberately — an inert knob is a silent lie): operator registry via `SCARAB_RETENTION_CONFIG_FILE` (bad file = boot failure), pipeline-level `retention_profile:` key riding `runs.ir`, per-run cutoffs resolved against the *current* registry at sweep time and re-resolved inside each victim transaction. The registry helper is shared with placement lookup, zero behavior change there.\n- `ExpiryPass::LockBusy` distinct from \"ran, nothing eligible\" — an early suite flake (hypothesis disproven empirically: advisory locks are per-database) can now only resurface as a *named* failure.\n\nReview follow-up filed as `a543fef`: the nomination window can starve behind ≥100 long-TTL runs (liveness only, retention-safe direction) — per-run cutoff into SQL or keyset pagination, plus a floor index.\n\nA rerun of a retention-expired run must re-derive its ancestors or fail loudly on reads — that is retention semantics, not a race, and the `RerunPlan` doc now says so (the `4afaa3e` rider).\n\nCloses `6499fb1` and `82c5775` on merge.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n---\n\n\n**@thulasi-ram** — 2026-08-26T12:11:29Z\n\nPost-review fix pushed (`9e09042`): the intermittent `the_reachability_floor_gates_pre_epoch_victims_only` failure was a real clock-authority bug in this PR, not a flake — `depot_packs.created_at` was stamped from the host's `now_secs()` while the epoch row uses Postgres `now()` (~0.15s skew on colima, 7/25 repro at the branch tip). A pack staged in the skew window classified pre-epoch and parked behind the reachability floor; production shape: boot-adjacent drains silently defer. Both pack-row INSERTs now stamp from `EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM now())` — the one-clock rule this PR's own expiry pass states. 0/25 repro after; full suite 911/911 rerun on the branch. Found by the warm-bound work (cba7165) stacking on this branch — its suite run surfaced the deterministic case.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}